## Automated AI review

> **Community review:** Independent automated community review, unaffiliated with the Omarchy team, intended to help prepare PRs for their review.

**Outcome:** `toggleOutputMute()` now flips the mute and can flip it straight back, so the output mute toggle can do nothing.

### Output mute toggle reverts itself

It sets `volumeSink.audio.muted`, then runs `pactl set-sink-mute <sink> toggle`, which reads the new state and flips it back. With Quickshell 0.3.1 and PipeWire 1.6.8 on a null sink, 0 of 44 head calls changed the state (32 of 32 at the merge base). **Impact:** right-click on the output slider, `m`, Enter on its row; card-backed sinks (speakers, Bluetooth) depend on timing, untested.

**Suggested change:** compute `var mute = !outputMuted`, assign it to `volumeSink.audio.muted` and pass `mute ? "1" : "0"` to pactl, like `toggleAllMuted()`.

