# toggleOutputMute() flips the output twice

Reviewed head: `1e703c922d902f1c70d68931da778d5a86a291d7` (merge base `b679363bed05415771a1b1dc92c6899a908236f7`).

## Test in the repository's style

Save as `test/shell.d/audio-output-mute-test.sh` and run `bash test/shell.d/audio-output-mute-test.sh`. It runs the real `toggleOutputMute()` text from `Panel.qml` against a fake sink. The fake applies the Quickshell property write at once and runs the spawned `pactl` command afterwards, reading the current state for `toggle` the way `pactl` does. That is the order observed in the runtime check below.

```bash
#!/bin/bash

set -euo pipefail

source "$(cd -- "$(dirname -- "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)/base-test.sh"

run_node_test <<'JS'
const fs = require('fs')
const panel = fs.readFileSync(path.join(root, 'shell/plugins/panels/audio/Panel.qml'), 'utf8')

// Pull a top-level function out of Panel.qml so it can run against a fake sink.
function panelFunction(name, names) {
  const start = panel.indexOf(`  function ${name}(`)
  if (start < 0) fail(`Panel.qml defines ${name}`)
  const end = panel.indexOf('\n  }\n', start)
  return new Function(...names, `${panel.slice(start, end + 4)}\nreturn ${name}`)
}

// One sink as the audio server sees it. Quickshell's property write reaches the
// server before a spawned pactl has connected, so the fake applies it at once and
// runs spawned pactl commands afterwards, reading server state the way pactl does
// for `toggle`.
function world(muted) {
  const server = { muted }
  const spawned = []
  const volumeSink = {
    name: 'alsa_output.test',
    audio: {
      get muted() { return server.muted },
      set muted(value) { server.muted = value }
    }
  }
  const Quickshell = { execDetached: argv => spawned.push(argv) }
  const runSpawned = () => {
    for (const argv of spawned) {
      if (argv[0] !== 'pactl' || argv[1] !== 'set-sink-mute') continue
      server.muted = argv[3] === 'toggle' ? !server.muted : argv[3] === '1'
    }
  }
  return { server, volumeSink, Quickshell, runSpawned }
}

const names = ['volumeSink', 'volumeSinkName', 'Quickshell', 'outputMuted']
for (const start of [false, true]) {
  const w = world(start)
  const toggleOutputMute = panelFunction('toggleOutputMute', names)(w.volumeSink, 'alsa_output.test', w.Quickshell, start)
  toggleOutputMute()
  w.runSpawned()
  assertEqual(w.server.muted, !start, `toggleOutputMute ${start ? 'unmutes a muted' : 'mutes an unmuted'} output`)
}
JS
```

### Actual output

At the PR head `1e703c92` (exit 1):

```
expected: true
actual:   false
not ok - toggleOutputMute mutes an unmuted output
```

At the merge base `b679363b` (exit 0):

```
ok - toggleOutputMute mutes an unmuted output
ok - toggleOutputMute unmutes a muted output
```

At the head with the suggested change applied (exit 0):

```
ok - toggleOutputMute mutes an unmuted output
ok - toggleOutputMute unmutes a muted output
```

The suggested change used for that run:

```diff
   function toggleOutputMute() {
-    if (volumeSink && volumeSink.audio) volumeSink.audio.muted = !volumeSink.audio.muted
+    var mute = !outputMuted
+    if (volumeSink && volumeSink.audio) volumeSink.audio.muted = mute
     var targetSink = volumeSinkName !== "" ? volumeSinkName : (volumeSink && volumeSink.name ? String(volumeSink.name) : "@DEFAULT_SINK@")
-    Quickshell.execDetached(["pactl", "set-sink-mute", targetSink, "toggle"])
+    Quickshell.execDetached(["pactl", "set-sink-mute", targetSink, mute ? "1" : "0"])
   }
```

The existing `test/shell.d/audio-test.sh` passes at both revisions (20 `ok` lines each); it only loads `Model.js`.

## Runtime check

Headless Quickshell 0.3.1 (Arch package, `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen`) against private PipeWire 1.6.8 and pipewire-pulse servers with one null sink, which Quickshell drives through node properties rather than a card route. The harness copies the `sink`/`volumeSink`/`outputMuted`/`anyAudible` declarations, the three changed functions and the `omarchy-audio-output-sink` process verbatim from each revision's `Panel.qml`, calls the functions over Quickshell IPC, and reads the sink with `pactl` 1 to 1.5 s later.

| Revision | `toggleOutputMute()` changed the mute state | `toggleAllMuted()` set the expected state |
|---|---|---|
| merge base `b679363b` | 32 of 32 calls | 10 of 10 |
| head `1e703c92` | 0 of 44 calls (each produced two sink change events) | 10 of 10 |
| head with the change above | 24 of 24 calls | 4 of 4 |

Quickshell's log for one head call:

```
  INFO quickshell.service.pipewire.node: Changed muted state of PwNode(0x789789ba0f00, id=19/bound) to true via node
  INFO quickshell.service.pipewire.node: Got updated mute status of PwNode(0x789789ba0f00, id=19/bound) - false
```

With arrival times recorded from `pactl subscribe`, the second (reverting) change event came 2.15 to 2.95 ms after the first in all 20 timed head calls.

Not tested: card-backed sinks (laptop speakers, headphones, HDMI, Bluetooth). There Quickshell 0.3.1 sends the mute through the device route, so the result depends on whether that write reaches pipewire-pulse before `pactl` reads the state.
