# setOutputVolume() flattens the channel balance (test)

Reviewed head: `1e703c922d902f1c70d68931da778d5a86a291d7` (merge base `b679363bed05415771a1b1dc92c6899a908236f7`).

## Test in the repository's style

Save as `test/shell.d/audio-output-balance-test.sh` and run `bash test/shell.d/audio-output-balance-test.sh`. It runs the real `setOutputVolume()` text from `Panel.qml` against a fake stereo sink. The fake models Quickshell's `audio.volume` setter (`PwNodeBoundAudio::setAverageVolume` in `src/services/pipewire/node.cpp`, Quickshell 0.3.1: every channel is scaled by new average over old average) and a spawned `pactl set-sink-volume` (`fill_volume()` in `src/utils/pactl.c`, PulseAudio 17.0: a single value is applied to every channel). The spawned command runs after the property write, matching the runtime check below, where the pactl value is the one that stayed. The test asserts that the right/left ratio survives.

```bash
#!/bin/bash

set -euo pipefail

source "$(cd -- "$(dirname -- "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)/base-test.sh"

run_node_test <<'JS'
const fs = require('fs')
const panel = fs.readFileSync(path.join(root, 'shell/plugins/panels/audio/Panel.qml'), 'utf8')

// Pull a top-level function out of Panel.qml so it can run against a fake sink.
function panelFunction(name, names) {
  const start = panel.indexOf(`  function ${name}(`)
  if (start < 0) fail(`Panel.qml defines ${name}`)
  const end = panel.indexOf('\n  }\n', start)
  return new Function(...names, `${panel.slice(start, end + 4)}\nreturn ${name}`)
}

// One stereo sink as the audio server sees it, with channel volumes on the
// scale Quickshell's audio.volume and pactl percentages share.
function world(volumes) {
  const server = { volumes: volumes.slice() }
  const spawned = []
  const audio = {
    get volume() {
      return server.volumes.reduce((sum, v) => sum + v, 0) / server.volumes.length
    },
    // Quickshell's setter (PwNodeBoundAudio::setAverageVolume in
    // src/services/pipewire/node.cpp): scale every channel by new / old average,
    // or set them all to the value when the old average is 0; negatives clamp to 0.
    set volume(value) {
      const old = this.volume
      const mul = old === 0 ? 0 : value / old
      server.volumes = server.volumes.map(v => Math.max(0, mul === 0 ? value : v * mul))
    }
  }
  const volumeSink = { name: 'alsa_output.test', audio }
  const Quickshell = { execDetached: argv => spawned.push(argv) }
  // A spawned `pactl set-sink-volume <sink> <values...>` lands after the property
  // write. One value is applied to every channel (fill_volume() in
  // src/utils/pactl.c); otherwise there must be one value per channel.
  const runSpawned = () => {
    for (const argv of spawned) {
      if (argv[0] !== 'pactl' || argv[1] !== 'set-sink-volume') continue
      const values = argv.slice(3).map(v => parseFloat(v) / 100)
      if (values.length === 1) server.volumes = server.volumes.map(() => values[0])
      else if (values.length === server.volumes.length) server.volumes = values
      else fail('pactl channel count matches the sink', argv.join(' '))
    }
  }
  return { server, volumeSink, Quickshell, runSpawned }
}

const pct = v => `${Math.round(v * 100)}%`
const names = ['volumeSink', 'volumeSinkName', 'Quickshell', 'outputVolume']
for (const [left, right, target] of [[0.4, 0.6, 0.6], [0.3, 0.7, 0.3]]) {
  const w = world([left, right])
  const setOutputVolume = panelFunction('setOutputVolume', names)(w.volumeSink, 'alsa_output.test', w.Quickshell, w.volumeSink.audio.volume)
  setOutputVolume(target)
  w.runSpawned()
  const [l, r] = w.server.volumes
  assert(
    l > 0 && Math.abs(r / l - right / left) < 1e-6,
    `setOutputVolume(${target}) keeps a ${pct(left)}/${pct(right)} balance`,
    `expected: ${pct(left * target / ((left + right) / 2))}/${pct(right * target / ((left + right) / 2))}\nactual:   ${pct(l)}/${pct(r)}`
  )
}
JS
```

### Actual output

At the PR head `1e703c92` (exit 1; stdout empty, stderr):

```
expected: 48%/72%
actual:   60%/60%
not ok - setOutputVolume(0.6) keeps a 40%/60% balance
```

At the merge base `b679363b` (exit 0; stderr empty, stdout):

```
ok - setOutputVolume(0.6) keeps a 40%/60% balance
ok - setOutputVolume(0.3) keeps a 30%/70% balance
```

Both runs used Node v26.7.0 in a sandbox, with `shell/plugins/panels/audio` and `test/shell.d/base-test.sh` taken from each revision.

This test models Quickshell and pactl from their source. The runtime check (headless Quickshell 0.3.1, PipeWire 1.6.8, real `pactl`) gave the same values: 40%/60% set to 0.6 became 60%/60% at the head and 48%/72% at the merge base.
</details>

